    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45023" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐρυ-όδειᾰ</span></b> , ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span>) fem. Adj. used only in
		gen., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with broad ways</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of the earth (as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐρύπορος</span> of the sea), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθονὸς εὐρυοδείης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.635
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.453
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> epith.
			of Demeter at Scarpheia, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδος</span> by <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				396.24
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐρυεδής</span>.)</div>
